# oracle: SPC/E water box (4500 atoms): fix shake tol 1e-4 iter 20, nve for 20 steps of 1 fs: thermo rows and the final per-atom state
# oracle-inputs: w48sh_spce.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.8e-13, atoms 1.0e-10.
# oracle-tolerance: measured with native LAMMPS (black box) against the engine: thermo rows agree to 3e-8 relative and the per-atom x, v, f at step 20 to 1.4e-6 relative (scale max(1,|value|)); the per-atom check of the harness is 100 times rel, so this passes at rel 1e-7; the per-step solve (each cluster iterates until its largest multiplier update times dt^2 ftm2v is within tol) is the source of the match, and the step-0 setup agrees to 1e-12
units		real
atom_style	full
read_data	w48sh_spce.data
pair_style	lj/cut/coul/long 12.0 12.0
kspace_style	pppm 1.0e-4
pair_coeff	1 1 0.15535 3.166
pair_coeff	* 2 0.0000 0.0000
bond_style	harmonic
angle_style	harmonic
dihedral_style	none
improper_style	none
bond_coeff	1 1000.00 1.000
angle_coeff	1 100.0 109.47
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.0 0.0 1.0
neighbor        2.0 bin
fix             1 all shake 0.0001 20 0 b 1 a 1
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             20
